    "overrides": [
      "editor.findMatchForeground",
      "statusBarItem.warningForeground",
      "editorGutter.background",
      "sideBarSectionHeader.background",
      "list.hoverBackground",
      "scrollbar.shadow"
    ],
    "rationale": "All 48 calculated roles were reviewed against the rendered workbench, not just against the formulas. editor.findMatchForeground: The default falls back to editor.foreground, but findMatchBackground is warning at 45% alpha — a light foreground on a light composite. Replaced with in-family ink so the match label survives its own highlight. statusBarItem.warningForeground: The default borrows button.foreground, which is ink chosen for the primary button fill, not for a brass badge. Derived against the warning background instead. editorGutter.background: The gutter is a well in Ultra, not canvas. Falling back to editor.background erases the line-number rail; substrate keeps it one step below the code. sideBarSectionHeader.background: A 10% foreground mix lands too close to the sidebar body to satisfy the three-step focus ladder. Crest is a real elevation step, so a content-owning accordion header separates from both the body and a hovered row. list.hoverBackground: Defaulting hover to 45% of active selection puts it 15% from inactive selection at 60% — the same tint at three strengths. Hover becomes a neutral elevation change instead, leaving the brand tint to mean selection. scrollbar.shadow: Alpha over editor.background reads as grey haze on a lifted canvas rather than a shadow. A true black alpha keeps the scroll edge legible at every surface depth. The remaining 42 calculations preserve Ultra Dusk as written: the alpha-based find, bracket, diff and scrollbar derivations all inherit the correct semantic hue, and the widget fallbacks correctly collapse dropdown, suggest, hover and notification surfaces onto the single dialog depth this theme defines."
  }
}
